# All optional.

# The cloud hub. Default: ws://<page-host>:8000/ws
# VITE_WS_URL=ws://localhost:8000/ws

# The chat UI the webview surrogate iframe points at. A ?device=<bound id> is appended
# automatically. Default: http://localhost:5173
# VITE_CHAT_UI_URL=http://localhost:5173

# --- v12: SPEECH INPUT (Sarvam speech-to-text). Optional; its absence is not an error. ---
#
# Set this and the composer grows a microphone: tap, speak, and ~1.5s of silence ends the
# recording and drops the transcript in the box for you to read and Send. Leave it empty
# and the mic is disabled with a title that says exactly this — everything else about the
# surrogate is unchanged, and the text box works as it always has.
#
# Key: https://dashboard.sarvam.ai
#
# NOTE THE MISSING `VITE_` PREFIX, AND DO NOT ADD ONE.
#
# That prefix is the entire mechanism keeping this credential out of the JavaScript
# bundle. Vite exposes VITE_-prefixed variables to client code and refuses to expose the
# rest, so `VITE_SARVAM_API_KEY` would work exactly as well at runtime while shipping
# your key to every browser that loads the page. Unprefixed, it is read in Node by
# vite.config.ts, which proxies /api/stt to Sarvam and attaches the key server-side. The
# page is told only WHETHER a key exists, as a boolean. `scripts/verify_stt.mjs` fails
# if anyone reverses this.
#
# THE LIMITATION, so it isn't discovered on stage: that proxy is the DEV SERVER's. Voice
# input works under `npm run dev` and NOT under `vite preview` or a built bundle, where
# /api/stt is a 404 (the error message says so). Fine for a dev surrogate; if the mic
# ever has to work from a built bundle, the call moves to the cloud hub next to the
# fish.audio client.
#
# ALSO: getUserMedia needs a SECURE CONTEXT. `localhost:5175` is one. The LAN address
# this dev server also serves (host: true) is NOT, and there the mic is missing entirely
# rather than broken. Speak to it on localhost.
# SARVAM_API_KEY=
#
# Where the proxy points. Default https://api.sarvam.ai — override only to record or
# replay against a stand-in.
# SARVAM_BASE_URL=https://api.sarvam.ai
